  "instance_name": "free_stuff_politics_stereotype",
  "label": "Free Stuff Politics Stereotype",
  "description": "A common political stereotype that caricatures politicians, especially from the Democratic Party, as being overly focused on 'free stuff' (e.g., free college, free healthcare, free public transportation) as a central policy theme, often used sarcastically to imply they are trivializing complex policy debates or pandering to populist demands. This stereotype is frequently used in political satire and media commentary to mock candidates perceived as prioritizing populist promises over substantive policy.",
